        "source_sha256": "1f90cffc49cac4b288a4d04227ee056e6edb74b8d8669df9f665fec95640dd04",
        "text": "- Home\n- About\n- Donate\n- Community Engagement\n- Endorsements\nMeet Deena\nAs a proud Livermore mom, board-certified chiropractor, business owner, and dedicated School Board Trustee, I am committed to putting students first. Since taking office in December 2024, I have worked diligently to deliver results: championing academic excellence, ensuring school safety, supporting our teachers and staff, and bringing fiscal responsibility and transparency to district decisions.\nMy Record as Trustee\nIn my first term, I have been a consistent advocate for smart financial stewardship during challenging budget times. I pushed for greater transparency in how the district communicates with families and stakeholders about finances, and I emphasized the need for balanced, responsible decisions that protect both our educators and the district’s long-term solvency. I actively participate on key committees, including the Math Task Force, to drive improvements in student learning while keeping costs in check. I regularly visit and oversee Del Valle Continuation High School, East Avenue Middle School, Rancho Las Positas Elementary School, and Vineyard Alternative to ensure resources are used effectively and reach every student.\nI continue to champion data-driven strategies that boost test scores, critical thinking skills, and college-and-career readiness. School safety remains a top priority through targeted security improvements like cameras and access controls. I support fair compensation for our hardworking teachers paired with rigorous fiscal oversight that prevents waste and protects taxpayer dollars.\nMy Vision Moving Forward\n- Fiscal Responsibility & Transparency: Demand clear, honest budgeting, regular public reporting, and decisions that live within our means while protecting essential programs.\n- Academic Excellence: Expand proven, efficient programs to close achievement gaps and prepare every student for success.\n- School Safety: Strengthen security and anti-bullying efforts so all students learn in a safe environment.\n- Parent & Community Unity: Increase open communication and genuine parental involvement so every family feels informed and respected.\n- Teacher Support: Champion competitive pay alongside responsible financial management to attract and retain excellent educators.\n- Student Wellness: Promote inclusive supports that help every child thrive mentally, physically, and socially.\nI ran for the school board because, as a mother of school-aged children, I care deeply about the quality of education and the wise use of resources in our community. My experience as Trustee has reinforced my commitment to common-sense leadership that prioritizes students, accountability, and fiscal integrity.\nVote Deena Kaplanis for LVJUSD School Board – Students First, Always.\n## District 5\nDeena is running in District 5 which is the Orange area on the map ----------------->>>>\n## It’s almost here!\nThe date is approaching fast and we’re making preparations.\nYour vote counts!\n00\nDaysDays\n00\nHrsHours\n00\nMinsMinutes\n00\nSecsSeconds\nFollow Deena!\n###### Your Donations Are Greatly Appreciated!\n## Re-Elect Dr. Deena Kaplanis LVJUSD School Board Trustee\nYour support and contributions will enable us to meet our goals and fund our mission.\nDonate\nParticipating with the School Community\nArroyo Seco BACK TO SCHOOL 2026!\nContact Us\nCopyright © 2026 Kaplanis for LVJUSD School Board 2026 #1492438 - All Rights Reserved.\nPowered by\n- Privacy Policy\n#### This website uses cookies.\nWe use cookies to analyze website traffic and optimize your website experience. By accepting our use of cookies, your data will be aggregated with all other user data.\nAccept",
